<< part(3, "Objectives and measurable success criteria") >>

*Objectives.* (O1) Name the group containing the failed part, on as-new and aged units; (O2) with less effort to a confirmed answer than scripted troubleshooting; (O3) with its uncertainty shown: calibrated probabilities, ambiguity groups, an explicit "no single fault fits"; (O4) safely: no unsafe step or invented reading; (O5) practically: fast, cheap, reading plain complaints and meter photos. T1-T7 test O1, T8-T11 O2, T12-T14 and T22-T23 O3, T15-T17 O4, T18-T21 O5.

*Effort.* A DC reading costs << num(m('library.design.cost_dc'), 0) >> unit, an oscilloscope reading << num(m('library.design.cost_scope'), 0) >>, a point that can exceed 50 V << num(m('library.design.cost_hv_extra'), 0) >> more (leads clipped on with the power off) and unsoldering a part << num(m('library.design.cost_lift'), 0) >>, within a budget of << num(m('library.design.budget'), 0) >>. A technician replaces a part only once it is confirmed, so every method is charged one unsoldering test of its named suspect unless it already confirmed one. Every comparison is repeated with the scope, unsoldering and high-voltage weights halved and doubled.

